    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: Active SBQQ__ProcessInput__c objects that have no input prompts.
Why it matters: A guided-selling flow with no inputs presents the rep with an empty wizard — they bypass it entirely and lose the value of the structured discovery flow. Often a sign of a broken or abandoned migration.
Suppress a finding: when the process exists as a placeholder pending business approval to add prompts.
Disable the detector: only if your org doesn&apos;t use guided selling. Most CPQ orgs that have configured it should leave this on.</value></values>
